  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-127078",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9927bff1-c245-542b-8d5d-fa7d24188b85",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given in Canonical Form",
      "problem": "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y+8}{-4}=\\frac{z+1}{11}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y-(-8)}{-4}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{11},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(10,-8,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨7,-4,11⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-8-4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "None of the listed",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-8-4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-4-8t \\\\ z=-1-11t\\end{aligned}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=8+4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-7-8t \\\\ z=-1+t\\end{aligned}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-127078",
        "kp_title": "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given in Canonical Form",
        "kp_href": null
      },
      "topic_id": 1799,
